    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "37bc288be21ecbb60bfc147fa19f1b290d1b7d0342b88d196f518b9550c82a1a",
      "text": "Breakfast at hotel.\n\nDeparts to Teotihuacan, about 60km northeast of the capital. Visit here the most impressing archaeological site of the central highlands: Teotihuacán (UNESCO World Cultural Heritage) surprises with the citadel, the Quetzalcoatl Temple, the Road of the Dead, Pyramids of the Sun and the Moon, as well as the Palace of Quetzalpapalotl and the Jaguar Temple. Do not miss the inspiring prehispanic paintings, hidden in some of the less visited parts of the site. Continue to Tulpetlac at the Parish of San Bernardino place of the 6th apparition of Our Lady of Guadalupe.\n\nBack to Mexico City and to Square of the Three Cultures and the Church of St. James. Mass\n\nBack to your hotel for overnight. Diner at hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1x6Whg-o3bJ1VGwgCJxq34Jl5roVLZq1b",
